{"abstract":[{"text":"Marks this host list as a standalone login screen rather than a sub-sheet of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"another login screen. This is the case in the forced-advanced-auth path, where","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the host list is the screen the user lands on and SFLoginViewController (which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"would otherwise own this chrome) is never created.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"presentedAsLoginScreen"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"kind":"text","text":" { "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"get"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"set"},{"kind":"text","text":" }"}],"platforms":["iOS","iPadOS","Mac Catalyst"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When set, this screen takes on the chrome that normally lives on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"SFLoginViewController: the navigation-bar back button (shown when there is an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"account or flow to return to) and the dev-only gear \/ “Login Options” menu."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The two are gated independently — the back button by the account\/flow logic in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"-shouldShowBackButton, the gear by dev-support being enabled — this flag only"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"distinguishes the standalone-screen role from the sub-sheet role."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Defaults to NO so the transient “Choose Connection” sub-sheet and the IdP flow,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","